libxkbcommon turns keyboard layouts (from xkeyboard-config) into keymaps and keysym
handling for wayland compositors and clients. Built without X11, wayland, docs, the
xkbcli tools and the layout registry (which would need libxml2). Needs bison to build,
which the base system provides. Installs libxkbcommon, headers and xkbcommon.pc under
/usr/local; keyboard data is read from /usr/local/share/X11/xkb.
upstream: https://xkbcommon.org/
